{
  "description": "R5: typing each of the 20 golden queries makes the a11y rows' top matches equal the golden table (probe.py rank(), name+uri), lists only subsequence matches with every decoy absent, and a 50-key script re-filters 5,000+ links with p99 < 16 ms",
  "requirement": "R5 (GPUI Phase 1)",
  "notes": [
    "Corpus: graph-ranking.json seeded into the graph. Expected tops: ranking-golden.json, whose order is probe.py's normative rank() (fixtures/README.md). The row count per query is len(rank(query)): non-matches on both name and uri are dropped, never ranked.",
    "Queries are typed into the filter as keystrokes through GPUI's own key dispatch (the filter input is focused when the browser opens, README contract) and cleared with Backspace, one per character.",
    "Each query is a block; rows are matched by URI and by name in their subtree (deep).",
    "The timing half seeds graph-5000.json on top (5,022 links) and reopens the browser. view.filter_samples / view.filter_p99_ms are the view's own per-keystroke re-filter timings since it was opened (README 'Phase 1 view-state contract'); 0 samples before typing proves they are per-open, not left over.",
    "Typing script: ('resource' then 8 Backspaces) x 3, then 'r', Backspace = 50 keystrokes, each one changing the filter text."
  ],
  "setup": {
    "graph": "graph-ranking.json"
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "graph": true,
      "resource_count": 22,
      "link_count": 0
    },
